"""golden-run RECIPE --repo EXPERIMENTAL_IMAGE_REPOSITORY: GG-first assembly in an isolated VZ builder.

Opt-in: --from-overlays --overlay-system ROOT materialises the set on the host first (pipeline/materialize.py, its
edit-engine store in store/cache/edit-engine-store, or --overlay-store, so unchanged specs and inputs are reused) and
plans which recipes install their files from the overlays instead of running their hooks (pipeline/overlays.py);
ROOT is the build's Golden Gate file system (its filesystem.dmg attached read-only), whose files the edits start
from. Every other recipe, and every step only the target can make, runs its hook as without the flag.

golden-gate-userspace's sealed cryptex images are kept in store/cache/cryptex, keyed on everything that decides their
bytes (its src/cryptex_cache.py), and copied instead of rebuilt when a build has the same key; --no-cryptex-cache
always builds them.

Every hook and post (in the VM, and wherever the kit is assembled) gets the assembly's target in its environment:
HAO_TARGET_MODEL (pipeline/targets/TARGET.json "model") and HAO_TARGET_DATA (the kit's target-data.json, the
target's "platform_data", {} when it has none)."""
